{
 "id": "a02",
 "label": "A2",
 "title": "Cooking terms",
 "summary": "Twenty kitchen verbs with the book's example sentences (ihurnó, batihín, pakuluín, pritúhin, igisá…) and the popular Filipino dishes: adóbo, sinigáng, lechón, lumpiá, hálo-halò and more",
 "minutes": 35,
 "goals": [
  "Understand how Filipino cooking mixes foreign and local influences",
  "Use twenty cooking verbs such as pakuluín (boil), pritúhin (fry) and igisá (sauté)",
  "Read the book's kitchen sentences and the words inside them",
  "Know the popular dishes and delicacies found on every Filipino table",
  "Know what merienda, karinderia and turo-turò are"
 ],
 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "Filipino cooking: a fusion",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "Filipino food has taken cooking methods, ingredients and whole dishes from **China, Spain, Mexico and the United States**, then each region of the Philippines gave them its own local taste."
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "culture",
     "title": "Food as history",
     "t": "The late teacher and food critic **Doreen Fernandez** described the Filipino kitchen as the result of the history and society that brought dishes in, the people who adapted them to their own tastes, and the culture that blended them into today's Filipino food. So Filipino food today is, in a way, Philippine history on a plate."
    },
    {
     "type": "p",
     "t": "The list below gives the Tagalog for twenty cooking actions, each with one of the book's sentences. Look for the familiar markers: [[ang|marker]] marks the thing being cooked, [[ng|marker]] and [[sa|marker]] add the other details."
    },
    {
     "type": "box",
     "kind": "tip",
     "title": "List word and sentence word",
     "t": "Some sentences use a different form of the verb from the one in the list. Compare: banlián (blanch) → **Binanlián** ko = I blanched; iháwin (broil) → **Iníhaw** ko = I broiled; tunawin (melt) → **Tinúnaw** ni Ana = Ana melted; ibábad (marinate) → **Ibabábad** ko = I will marinate."
    }
   ]
  },
